Z||000024||Sage||11-29-1999||12:12 PM||||Chadman: I have an 87GT white diamond pearl.  My wife drives an 84SE red.  My oldest son has an 86Gt(cuurently off road). My youngest son has an 88Coupe red.  My wife also has an 86GT silver, but am having trouble getting a title for it.  If anyone has any suggestions on this matter, I would appreciate your comments.  We bought the car from a towing service in Parkersburg, WV.  They picked it up for the cops after some kind of raid and siezure. The cops did not want to pay the tow bill, so they gave the guy the car.  He originally said he would have a title in 2 weeks.  That was May.  Been getting the run-around ever since.  Drove it on temp tags for 60 days,but now it is kind of useless to me as we can't put tags on it, and we can't sell it.  It is way too good for a parts car.  In the first 2 weeks we had it(when we were expecting to get a title), put a new alternator, new brakes all around, new ign. module, and new center console in.  Magistrate court in WV says we can press charges if he doesn't get us a title or refund our money, but that really doesn't serve any purpose as far as the car goes.  Anybody know of another avenue to investigate?  As for the white coupe in Marietta, I have seen several.  There is one really nice one that an older man drives, the rest that I have seen are kinda ragged out.  Who is your uncle, and where does he live?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
